From 78097488050c4357840a2b3c85e02feb32c4d458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mokomis <24596443+Mokomis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: carry the three reconnect-fix.3 parts upstream still
 lacks

- The virtual-display keepalive pinger parks between pings and is woken on
  stop, so the last slot's teardown no longer waits up to watchdog/3 s.
- The 1 s drain window before close is cut short when the session was
  stopped (preempted or reconnecting).
- On Windows, a silent loopback sink is polled every 100 ms instead of
  blocking up to 5 s, so a stopped session releases its capture promptly.

The reconnect wait itself is upstream's wait_released and is not changed.
Ported from patchsets/0.42.0-reconnect-fix.3 for personal use.
